1
00:00:03,400 --> 00:00:08,091
Freelancers get paid late. Buyers paying strangers get scammed.

2
00:00:07,991 --> 00:00:13,329
Proofhold binds a payment PayPal already holds to a test both sides agreed to.

3
00:00:13,967 --> 00:00:16,647
The seller writes the brief in plain words.

4
00:00:16,547 --> 00:00:25,647
It becomes an acceptance test: counts, formats, resolution, a deadline, and a judgement line.

5
00:00:25,547 --> 00:00:27,438
One link goes to the buyer.

6
00:00:35,433 --> 00:00:43,153
The buyer reads the same sheet and approves a PayPal authorization, not a payment.

7
00:00:43,053 --> 00:00:49,424
PayPal holds the money. Proofhold never does.

8
00:00:59,833 --> 00:01:07,762
The seller delivers through Proofhold. Validators measure the files.

9
00:01:07,662 --> 00:01:16,609
The examiner judges only what a machine cannot, and may abstain.

10
00:01:17,267 --> 00:01:25,671
The buyer confirms. PayPal captures. The seal is stamped.

11
00:01:26,733 --> 00:01:36,540
Every hold in one ledger. Objections go to review; a declined offer returns the money.

12
00:01:36,440 --> 00:01:45,400
After capture, PayPal decides. Proofhold files the evidence bundle.

13
00:01:45,300 --> 00:01:50,794
A printable record is the receipt.

14
00:01:51,433 --> 00:02:02,906
What is real, simulated and unproven is on screen, on every page.

15
00:02:02,806 --> 00:02:06,077
github.com/successaje/proofhold
